## Import files

The Warewulf system includes functionality to import arbitrary files from the
provisioning server for distribution to managed hosts through a system called
"overlays". Some files, like `/etc/passwd`, and `/etc/hosts` handled in this way
by default.  Here we add directories and files to the `nodesconfig` overlay that
is applied to all nodes.

The SSH host keys come in the runtime overlay, which `wwclient` applies on the
node. With two-stage provisioning the node's initramfs applies it first, before
systemd starts; when the node boots in one stage from iPXE, `wwclient` is the
first to apply it. A systemd drop-in has sshd and its host key generation start
after `wwclient`, so sshd serves the host keys from the head node rather than
new ones. With two-stage provisioning it delays sshd by a few seconds.

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_comment Import files -->
```bash
# Add the following to support unprivileged user namespaces for tools like Apptainer
wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig /etc/subuid
wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig /etc/subgid

# Identify head node as local NTP server, configure it with a template with a Tag
wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig \
 /opt/ohpc/pub/examples/chrony.conf.ww /etc/chrony.conf.ww
wwctl profile set --yes nodes --tagadd ntpserver="${sms_ip}"

# Configure systemd and NetworkManger to wait for the network to be fully up.
wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig \
 /opt/ohpc/pub/examples/network/NetworkManager-wait-online.service.d/override.conf \
 /etc/systemd/system/NetworkManager-wait-online.service.d/override.conf

# Start sshd after wwclient has applied the runtime overlay (SSH host keys)
mkdir -p /opt/ohpc/admin/warewulf
printf '[Unit]\nWants=wwclient.service\nAfter=wwclient.service\n' \
	> /opt/ohpc/admin/warewulf/wait-wwclient.conf
for unit in sshd.service sshd-keygen@.service; do
	wwctl overlay import --parents nodeconfig \
		/opt/ohpc/admin/warewulf/wait-wwclient.conf \
		/etc/systemd/system/${unit}.d/wait-wwclient.conf
done
```
<!-- ohpc_end -->
